      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "It's possible to simulate `nodes[1]` not running with the following diff on 8130b3b8836879915e82730eb818ee6b58c28168:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/test/functional/p2p_tx_download.py b/test/functional/p2p_tx_download.py\r\nindex aa43cc18e2..4a83e44b91 100755\r\n--- a/test/functional/p2p_tx_download.py\r\n+++ b/test/functional/p2p_tx_download.py\r\n@@ -116,6 +116,8 @@ class TxDownloadTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\r\n         self.log.info(\"Put the tx in node 0's mempool\")\r\n         self.nodes[0].sendrawtransaction(tx['hex'])\r\n \r\n+        time.sleep(2)\r\n+\r\n         # Since node 1 is connected outbound to an honest peer (node 0), it\r\n         # should get the tx within a timeout.\r\n         # However, node 0 sees the same connection as inbound, so it may not\r\n```",
      "user": {
        "login": "Crypt-iQ",
        "id": 15145615,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTQ1NjE1",
