      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I tested the master and PR versions using the same binary and Crypt-iQ's reproducer, adding a delay after `sendrawtransaction`.\n\nOn master, with a 2-second delay, 2/5 runs failed due to mempool sync timeouts. With the PR, both runs passed. Increasing the delay to 5 seconds made master pass, but runs took around 83 seconds instead of 26, while the PR remained around 26 seconds.\n\nLooking at node1's debug log, master requests the wtx from peer 4, which never responds, and retries node0 only after 60 seconds. With the PR, it requests from peer 0 almost immediately after receiving the inventory. So this isn't just fixing a flaky test; it also avoids a silent 60-second slowdown when the race occurs.\n",
